<title>SOUTH AFRICA: M-CELL SWINGS INTO PROFIT AT HALF-YEAR.</title>
<headline>M-CELL SWINGS INTO PROFIT AT HALF-YEAR.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30.</p>
<p>Comparative figures for nine months ended March 31.</p>
<p>			  (million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr		    3.2 cts	  vs 0.3 cts loss</p>
<p>    Div		     -		     -</p>
<p>    Attrib profit     15.7		vs 9.8 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax	     18.7		vs 6.6 loss</p>
<p>    Tax		    3.0		vs 3.2</p>
<p>    Finance income     5.1		vs 10.3</p>
<p>    Turnover	   237.7		vs 254.3 </p>
<p>Full name: M-Cell Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The cellular telephone company did not declare a</p>
<p>dividend.</p>
<p>Comparative figures were for the nine months to March 31,</p>
<p>because it commenced operations on June 30, 1995.</p>
<p>Directors said the cellular telephone market in South Africa</p>
<p>continued to experience remarkable growth and they expected this</p>
<p>to continue for the next few years before the market matures.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom -27-11-482.1003</p>
</text>
